</div>

@code {
    private CongregationProfile _profile = new();

    private IReadOnlyList<FoundationSummaryDto> _items = [];

    [Parameter] public string Slug { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    protected override async Task OnParametersSetAsync()
    {
        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Slug))
        {
            TenantContext.SetSlug(Slug);
        }
        _profile = await CongregationService.GetCurrentAsync();
        _items = await Queries.ListAsync();
    }

    private static string GetFeastTag(int? order) => order switch
    {
        7 => "Passover, Unleavened Bread & Weeks (Spring Feasts)",
        8 => "The 2nd Exodus (Grafted in by Blood & Spirit)",
        9 => "Feast of Trumpets (Messiah Returns to Reign)",
        10 => "Day of Atonement (Satan Bound)",
        11 => "Feast of Tabernacles (Millennial Kingdom)",
        12 => "The 8th Day (The Eternal Kingdom)",
        _ => string.Empty
    };

    private record HookData(string Mystery, string TraditionVsTruth, string KeyVerses);

    private static HookData GetHookInfo(int? order) => order switch
    {
        1 => new(
            "Adam was given dominion as king and priest over a physical earth. The Fall wasn't just personal guilt—it was the loss of the Kingdom of God on earth.",
            "Churches teach salvation is about leaving earth to live in the clouds with a harp. The Bible teaches that God's ultimate plan is restoring paradise ON EARTH (Matt 5:5; Rev 21:2).",
            "Genesis 1:26-28; Genesis 3:15; Matthew 5:5; Revelation 21:1-4"
        ),
        2 => new(
            "The Global Flood was a divine legal baptism of the entire planet. God did not destroy the earth; He cleansed it with water and preserved a righteous remnant to inherit the new beginning.",
            "People treat Noah as a fairy tale and misapply Jesus' words: the wicked were 'taken away' in judgment, while the righteous were left behind on the cleansed earth (Matt 24:37-41).",
            "Genesis 6-9; 1 Peter 3:20-21; 2 Peter 3:5-7; Matthew 24:37-39"
        ),
        3 => new(
            "Under Nimrod, humanity built a one-world religious, political, and economic headquarters at Babel. When God scattered their languages, the seeds of the Babylonian mystery religion spread to every continent.",
            "Babylon is not an extinct ancient ruin. It is an active false religious system that infiltrated church tradition, replacing God's Sabbath and Feasts with pagan solstice rituals (Rev 17-18).",
            "Genesis 10:8-10; Genesis 11:1-9; Revelation 17:5; Revelation 18:4"
        ),
        4 => new(
            "God answered Babylon by calling Abraham and entering into a wedding covenant at Mount Sinai with the 12 tribes of Israel, taking them as His holy nation and covenant bride.",
            "Replacement Theology claims God 'divorced and discarded Israel' to create a Gentile church. Scripture declares God's covenant with Israel is everlasting (Jer 31:35-37; Rom 11:1-2).",
            "Genesis 12:1-3; Exodus 19:5-6; Jeremiah 3:14; Romans 11:17-24"
        ),
        5 => new(
            "After Solomon, Israel split into two nations: the Southern House of Judah (Jews) and the Northern House of Israel (10 tribes). The Northern Kingdom was exiled into the nations and became 'lost sheep' (Hosea 1:9).",
            "Most Christians don't know the difference between a Jew (tribe of Judah) and an Israelite (12 tribes). Understanding the two houses is the master key to Paul's epistles and Romans 9-11.",
            "1 Kings 11:30-31; 2 Kings 17:22-23; Hosea 1:9-10; Matthew 15:24"
        ),
        6 => new(
            "Old Testament prophets gave over 300 precise prophecies predicting both the Suffering Servant (Messiah ben Joseph) and the Ruling King (Messiah ben David), and the promise of a New Covenant.",
            "The New Covenant is not a brand new religion discarding God's Law. It is made specifically with the House of Israel and Judah (Jer 31:31), writing God's Torah on our hearts.",
            "Isaiah 9:6-7; Isaiah 53; Jeremiah 31:31-34; Ezekiel 37:15-28"
        ),
        7 => new(
            "Yeshua came proclaiming the royal Gospel of the Kingdom of God. In His First Coming, He fulfilled the 4 Spring Feasts to the exact day: Passover (death), Unleavened Bread (burial), Firstfruits (resurrection), and Weeks (Spirit).",
            "Jesus never preached 'accept me to go to heaven when you die.' He preached: 'Repent, for the Kingdom of God is at hand!' (Mark 1:14-15; Matt 4:23).",
            "Mark 1:14-15; 1 Corinthians 5:7; 1 Corinthians 15:20; Acts 2:1-4"
        ),
        8 => new(
            "Jesus said He was sent to the lost sheep of the House of Israel. Through the Apostles, the scattered Israelites among the Gentiles are found and grafted back into the commonwealth of Israel by Blood, Water, and Spirit.",
            "Gentile believers are not a separate church entity from Israel. Through faith in Messiah, they are grafted into the one Olive Tree of Israel, sharing in the covenants of promise (Eph 2:11-19).",
            "Matthew 10:5-6; Acts 2:38-39; Ephesians 2:11-19; James 1:1; 1 Peter 1:1"
        ),
        9 => new(
            "Messiah is returning bodily to the Mount of Olives to reign over all the nations from Jerusalem for 1,000 years, fulfilling the Feast of Trumpets at the 7th trumpet (Rev 11:15).",
            "Popular rapture theories claim believers vanish off to heaven. The Bible promises that the saints will reign with King Jesus AS KINGS AND PRIESTS UPON THE EARTH (Rev 5:10; Rev 20:4-6).",
            "Acts 1:6-11; Zechariah 14:4-9; Revelation 11:15; Revelation 20:4-6"
        ),
        10 => new(
            "The final manifestation of Mystery Babylon—the global false religious, economic, and political system—is exposed, judged, and destroyed in one hour.",
            "Believers must heed God's urgent call: 'Come out of her, My people, lest you share in her sins and receive of her plagues' (Rev 18:4). We cannot compromise with Babylonian traditions.",
            "Revelation 14:8; Revelation 17:1-6; Revelation 18:1-10; Jeremiah 51:6"
        ),
        11 => new(
            "Just as the earth was cleansed with water at the Flood, the present heavens and earth will be purified by divine fire and Spirit, destroying the curse, disease, and death forever.",
            "The fire does not annihilate creation; it refines and purges away all corruption so that the righteous may dwell on a renewed earth in glory (2 Peter 3:10-13; Mal 4:1-3).",
